  "body": "## What\n\nAdd the case `examples/catalog/multiaxis/five-axis`: Swarf cuts a tilted wall. 5-Axis Contour and 5-Axis Flow cut a surface.\n\n## Notes\n\nMachine: `assets/machines/tilthead.mch` or a different 5-axis file. The case changes no check. A check that is wrong is a new bug.\n\nDone means: The case folder obeys `examples/catalog/README.md`: `model/` with its generator script, `build.camscript`, `<case>.camproj`, `<case>.nc` and `README.md`. The geometry is original (Clean-Room Protocol). `cargo xtask catalog --check` and `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog` pass. The README says what the case shows and what to look at. The collision check is clean. The case stays in its time budget, or it is in the heavy lane.\n\nFile each refusal or wrong output that the work finds as its own bug. Link the bug on #2392. A missing parameter in an MCP tool is a new `area:mcp` issue.\n\nPart of #2392\n",
